Pacyte Nexus v0.25.2 Alpha — Project Status Report

Date: May 31, 2026
Purpose: To objectively document the current state of the project, its strengths, weaknesses, and readiness level without proposing specific technical solutions.

---

1. Executive Summary

Pacyte Nexus is a Layer‑1 blockchain prototype written from scratch in Rust, consisting of 48,000+ lines of code. The project is currently in the Alpha (Proof of Concept) stage. All 11 modules compile with zero errors, and a functional node can be started. A significant architectural gap exists: the on‑chain distribution of the 250 million PNX Titan reward pool is not yet implemented in the Rust node. This gap does not prevent closed‑testnet operation, community building, or grant applications but must be addressed before a public testnet launch.

